What:		/sys/kernel/dmabuf/buffers/<inode_number>/exporter_name
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	Linux media mailing list <linux-media@vger.kernel.org>
Description:
		Read-only name of the DMA-BUF exporter, or "unknown" when no
		exporter name was supplied. Available with CONFIG_DMABUF_SYSFS_STATS.
		Entries are created asynchronously and disappear when the buffer
		is released; short-lived buffers may never appear.

What:		/sys/kernel/dmabuf/buffers/<inode_number>/size
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	Linux media mailing list <linux-media@vger.kernel.org>
Description:
		Read-only size of the DMA-BUF in bytes, as a decimal integer.
		The directory name is the inode number of its sharing file.
